      "id": 9230,
      "name": "danmarshall14",
      "username": "danmarshall14",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/danmarshall14/{size}/1944_2.png",
      "created_at": "2014-01-08T17:36:48.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>Forgive me if this has been answered before, but most redirection abilities use the text \"The first time so and so would be dealt damage...\"</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>More specifically for Amulet - The first time Nightmist would be dealt damage each turn, you may discard 2 cards. If you do, you may redirect that damage to a target of your choice</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Now, let's say a villain is going to deal me 1 damage at the End of Turn and one of his minions is going to deal me 3 damage after that.&nbsp; Could I let the villain hit me for 1 and then use my redirection on the 3 damage, even though the villain is dealing damage \"first\"?&nbsp; Or do I only have the option to redirect the first attack that turn, or none at all?</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Again, sorry if this has been answered; I did a search but most redirection topics are concerning other matters.</p>",
      "post_number": 1,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:39:57.545Z",
