      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/danmarshall14/{size}/1944_2.png",
      "created_at": "2014-01-08T21:48:13.000Z",
      "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Silverleaf\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/silverleaf/48/2332_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Silverleaf:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>When it says \"the first time\", it means \"the first time\". Not \"the first time you think it's worth it\". <img src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/images/emoji/apple/wink.png?v=12\" title=\":wink:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":wink:\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\"></p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Well this changes everything.&nbsp; That's how I was playing the entire game.&nbsp; \"Kismet deals everyone 2 psychic damage…if you think it's worth it.\"</p>\n<p>But, thanks for clearing it up; I had always assumed the \"first time\" text was there to keep people from redirecting every instance of damage during the turn.</p>",
